  "step_3": "The decision reason requires computing an aspiration level as the mean of all outcomes and then evaluating which lottery has a higher chance of exceeding this level. The aspiration level (1633.33) is not mentioned or implied in the verbal report. The individual does not discuss deviations from a reference point or threshold. Instead, they compare the lotteries directly in terms of prize size and probability, noting small differences. While they do consider probabilities and outcomes, the specific cognitive mechanism of an aspiration level and positive deviations from it is absent. There is no evidence that the individual structured their thinking around such a benchmark. The justification based on near-equivalence and spontaneity further suggests a lack of systematic evaluation consistent with the reason. Therefore, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
