{
  "step_1": "The decision reason is based on an aspiration level calculated as the mean of all outcomes in the decision problem, ignoring probabilities. The outcomes in the problem are: 4000, 0 (from Lottery B), and 3000 (from Lottery A). The mean of these outcomes is (4000 + 0 + 3000) / 3 = 2333.33 Euros. This is the aspiration level. The reason then evaluates each lottery by the probability of yielding an outcome above this level (i.e., positive difference). For Lottery A: outcome is 3000, which is above 2333.33 → positive difference; probability = 100%. For Lottery B: 4000 > 2333.33 (positive difference) with 80% probability; 0 < 2333.33 (negative difference) with 20% probability. Thus, Lottery A has a 100% chance of a positive difference, Lottery B has 80%. The reason would prefer Lottery A because it has a higher probability of exceeding the aspiration level.",
