  "step_3": "The decision reason requires computing an aspiration level as the mean of all outcomes (ignoring probabilities) and then comparing the probabilities of exceeding this level. The aspiration level (2333.33) and the comparison of probabilities of positive deviations (25% vs. 20%) are central. However, the individual does not mention any such calculation, reference point, or systematic comparison of outcomes relative to a mean. Instead, the individual emphasizes similarity, high chance of zero, and spontaneous decision-making. There is no indication that the individual computed or used an aspiration level or evaluated which lottery more frequently exceeds it. The justification is inconsistent with the reason’s rule, and the information required by the reason is not reflected in the report. Therefore, it is unlikely the individual used this reason.",
